															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/gg-crono" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(295496); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=295496&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608196105" alt="GG Crono" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=295496)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/gg-crono" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(295496); return false;" >GG Crono</a></span> <span class="odate time_1333412220 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">03 Apr 2012 00:17</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1408479">
									

<p>This is pretty good. However, the grammar is still a little shaky. For example, ellipses (that is, a &#8230;) should always be exactly three dots, and a few times, you have periods where there should be commas in dialogue that's immediately followed by more narration. For example:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;6 foot man eating chicken.&quot; came the reply, as calm and straight faced as the time of day.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The period after &quot;chicken&quot; should be a comma, in that case. And while we're on this subject, you should really have written the number out for a sentence of spoken dialogue like this one (i.e. &quot;six&quot; rather than &quot;6&quot;). It's okay for written dialogue, if you think that the one writing would be inclined to make that particular grammatical error.</p>
<p>I did like this enough to upvote it, but it needs a few firm whacks with the grammar stick. :)</p>

							</div>

								
